00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:32.800
Isn't that how--

00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:34.960
I mean, because you
have the holes and then

00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:39.920
the electrons on the side
creating the opposite pole

00:40:39.920 --> 00:40:40.590
electric field.

00:40:40.590 --> 00:40:42.850
Doesn't light hit the middle?

00:40:42.850 --> 00:40:45.040
I mean, that was
my understanding.

00:40:45.040 --> 00:40:47.240
I may be wrong, but I
thought it hit the middle.

00:40:50.210 --> 00:40:51.210
PROFESSOR: I'm not sure.

00:40:51.210 --> 00:40:53.040
That's not how I understood it.

00:40:55.920 --> 00:41:00.480
So the reason-- so the
absorption coefficient

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:03.820
of silicon is really low.

00:41:03.820 --> 00:41:06.810
So you have a lot of
different solar cells, right?

00:41:06.810 --> 00:41:09.060
You have amorphous silicon.

00:41:09.060 --> 00:41:13.930
You have multi-crystalline
silicon and stuff.

00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:15.510
And the reason why--

00:41:15.510 --> 00:41:17.200
you have thin film
cells as well.

00:41:17.200 --> 00:41:19.410
But the reason why
silicon cells are so thick

00:41:19.410 --> 00:41:22.260
is because the absorption
coefficient is so low

00:41:22.260 --> 00:41:24.510
that you basically
need a thicker

00:41:24.510 --> 00:41:30.730
area to be able to
absorb most of the light.

00:41:30.730 --> 00:41:32.730
I'm not answering
your question, am I?

00:41:32.730 --> 00:41:33.480
You think that--

00:41:33.480 --> 00:41:34.555
AUDIENCE: So my
understanding was

00:41:34.555 --> 00:41:35.430
that it would hit the middle--

00:41:35.430 --> 00:41:36.790
like, not exactly the middle.

00:41:36.790 --> 00:41:38.290
But you know how
like in the middle,

00:41:38.290 --> 00:41:39.832
you have the opposite
electric field?

00:41:39.832 --> 00:41:43.302
Because of the holes in
the electrons on the sides?

00:41:43.302 --> 00:41:44.010
PROFESSOR: Right.

00:41:44.010 --> 00:41:46.230
AUDIENCE: So if this is
your n and your peak,

00:41:46.230 --> 00:41:48.780
then you'd have volts here,
and you have electrons here

00:41:48.780 --> 00:41:50.640
from the opposite field.

00:41:50.640 --> 00:41:52.890
And my understanding was
that it would hit the middle,

00:41:52.890 --> 00:41:54.515
and the field would
